De:	Kevin Jones [SMTP:Kevin.Jones@compelsolve.co.uk]
Objet:	RE: HSG80 8.6 P - 5.1A : Fun whith PREFERRED_PATH

Emmanul=20

Unfortunately this is the expected (correct) behaviour. If the unit is =
to be
'served' by the preferred HSG80 controller, then the pair must be =
rebooted
together within a short time of each other (30 seconds I think). As you =
have
seen when one HSG80 in the pair is rebooted, the unit fails over to the
other HSG80 but does NOT fail back. The only way of making it fail back =
is
by use of the scu utility and forcing a start on the unit via a =
specific
bus, target, lun, unfortunately I have never seen the precise syntax =
for
doing this but I assume it will be in the scu man page.

Regards=20

Kevin Jones=20
